From 491585a618f9a2b4f4e25197bd366902f7c1a793 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Senn <roman.l.senn@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 19:21:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Populate wsi->udp->sa46 from sa46_peer on UDP client adopt

lws_create_adopt_udp2() (core-net/adopt.c) resolves the peer address
into a local `s->dest`, then tries `if (wsi->udp) wsi->udp->sa46 =
s->dest;` before falling back to the always-set `wsi->sa46_peer =
s->dest;`. For a client (connect()ing) UDP wsi, `wsi->udp` does not
exist yet at that point - it's allocated later, in
rops_adoption_bind_raw_skt() below, as part of
lws_adopt_descriptor_vhost2() - so that assignment is always a no-op
and wsi->udp->sa46 is left zeroed (AF_UNSPEC) by the memset() that
follows its allocation.

Later writes on that wsi (lws_ssl_capable_write_no_ssl(), in
core-net/output.c) call sendto() using sa46_sockaddr(&wsi->udp->sa46)
as the destination - passing that zeroed sockaddr to sendto() on an
already-connected socket, which glibc rejects with EINVAL instead of
using the connected peer.

Pick up the already-correct wsi->sa46_peer right after wsi->udp is
allocated, so sendto() gets a real destination.
---
 lib/roles/raw-skt/ops-raw-skt.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/roles/raw-skt/ops-raw-skt.c b/lib/roles/raw-skt/ops-raw-skt.c
index add7f654b..6130f113d 100644
--- a/lib/roles/raw-skt/ops-raw-skt.c
+++ b/lib/roles/raw-skt/ops-raw-skt.c
@@ -293,6 +293,16 @@ rops_adoption_bind_raw_skt(struct lws *wsi, int type, const char *vh_prot_name)
 		if (!wsi->udp)
 			return 0;
 		memset(wsi->udp, 0, sizeof(*wsi->udp));
+
+		/*
+		 * For a udp client wsi that just connect()ed, the peer
+		 * address was already resolved into wsi->sa46_peer (see
+		 * lws_create_adopt_udp2() in adopt.c) before this wsi->udp
+		 * existed to receive it directly.  Pick it up here so
+		 * sendto() has a real destination instead of an all-zero
+		 * AF_UNSPEC sockaddr.
+		 */
+		wsi->udp->sa46 = wsi->udp->sa46_pending = wsi->sa46_peer;
 	}
 #endif

